IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg7-governing-provisions`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, s 262(a), (b), (c) -- APPRAISAL RIGHTS: WHO IS ENTITLED, AND FOR WHICH SHARES.
-- Source: de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text); `-- src:N | ...` quotes line N.
--
-- Subsection (a) says who is entitled to an appraisal by the Court of Chancery; (b) says for which shares appraisal
-- rights are available as of right (and (b)(1), (2) and (3) are a proviso, an exception to it and a further case);
-- (c) lets a corporation's certificate of incorporation add events. Subsections (d) onward (perfecting, petition,
-- hearing, valuation) are in dg7-appraisal-procedure.l4 and dg7-appraisal-proceeding.l4.
--
-- OUT OF RANGE (taken as plain inputs, never imported): the vote or consent that s 228 describes (piece dg5), the
-- vote of surviving-corporation stockholders that s 251(f) describes (piece dg6), and which provision a transaction
-- is effected under (the transaction itself is encoded by pieces dg6, dg7 and dg8).
-- The section is "a stockholder's section": the person asking is a stockholder (or a beneficial owner) and the other
-- party of each relation is the surviving, resulting or converted entity and the Court of Chancery.

§ `s 262(a) The words that subsection (a) defines`

-- "As used in this section, the word stockholder means a holder of record of stock in a corporation".
-- src:1252 | As used in this section, the word “stockholder” means a holder of record of stock in a corporation …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(a) (src:1252)
GIVEN `the person is a holder of record` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holding is stock in a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(a) a stockholder` `the person is a holder of record` `the holding is stock in a corporation` MEANS
    `the person is a holder of record` AND `the holding is stock in a corporation`

-- "the words stock and share mean and include what is ordinarily meant by those words".
-- src:1252 | the words “stock” and “share” mean and include what is ordinarily meant by those words …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(a) (src:1252)
GIVEN `the thing is what is ordinarily meant by stock or share` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(a) stock or a share` `the thing is what is ordinarily meant by stock or share` MEANS
    `the thing is what is ordinarily meant by stock or share`

-- "the words depository receipt mean a receipt or other instrument issued by a depository representing an interest in
-- 1 or more shares, or fractions thereof, solely of stock of a corporation, which stock is deposited with the depository".
-- src:1252 | the words “depository receipt” mean a receipt or other instrument issued by a depository representing an interest in 1 or more shares, or fractions thereof, solely of stock of a corporation, which stock is deposited with the depository …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(a) (src:1252)
DECLARE `s 262(a) Instrument` HAS
    `it is a receipt or other instrument issued by a depository`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `it represents an interest in 1 or more shares, or fractions thereof`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the shares or fractions are solely of stock of a corporation`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `that stock is deposited with the depository`                                 IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1252 | the words “depository receipt” mean a receipt or other instrument issued by a depository representing an interest in 1 or more shares, or fractions thereof, solely of stock of a corporation, which stock is deposited with the depository …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(a) (src:1252)
GIVEN i IS A `s 262(a) Instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(a) a depository receipt` i MEANS
        i's `it is a receipt or other instrument issued by a depository`
    AND i's `it represents an interest in 1 or more shares, or fractions thereof`
    AND i's `the shares or fractions are solely of stock of a corporation`
    AND i's `that stock is deposited with the depository`

-- "the words beneficial owner mean a person who is the beneficial owner of shares of stock held either in voting trust
-- or by a nominee on behalf of such person".
-- src:1252 | the words “beneficial owner” mean a person who is the beneficial owner of shares of stock held either in voting trust or by a nominee on behalf of such person …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(a) (src:1252)
GIVEN `the person is the beneficial owner of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are held in voting trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are held by a nominee on behalf of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(a) a beneficial owner` `the person is the beneficial owner of the shares` `the shares are held in voting trust` `the shares are held by a nominee on behalf of the person` MEANS
        `the person is the beneficial owner of the shares`
    AND (   `the shares are held in voting trust`
         OR `the shares are held by a nominee on behalf of the person`)

-- "the word person means any individual, corporation, partnership, unincorporated association or other entity".
-- Every kind in the core's `Kind of entity` is an individual, a corporation, a partnership, an unincorporated
-- association or another entity, so the definition holds of all of them (the core's superset, KEEL fork F1).
-- src:1252 | and the word “person” means any individual, corporation, partnership, unincorporated association or other entity …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(a) (src:1252)
GIVEN e IS A `Kind of entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(a) a person` e MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `a natural person`                            THEN TRUE   -- any individual
    WHEN `a corporation` k                             THEN TRUE   -- corporation
    WHEN `a general partnership`                       THEN TRUE   -- partnership
    WHEN `a limited partnership`                       THEN TRUE   -- partnership
    WHEN `a limited liability partnership`             THEN TRUE   -- partnership
    WHEN `a limited liability limited partnership`     THEN TRUE   -- partnership
    WHEN `a joint-stock association`                   THEN TRUE   -- unincorporated association
    WHEN `any other unincorporated business or association` THEN TRUE   -- unincorporated association
    WHEN `a limited liability company`                 THEN TRUE   -- other entity
    WHEN `a statutory trust`                           THEN TRUE   -- other entity
    WHEN `a business trust or association`             THEN TRUE   -- other entity
    WHEN `a real estate investment trust`              THEN TRUE   -- other entity
    WHEN `a common-law trust`                          THEN TRUE   -- other entity

§ `s 262(a) Who is entitled to an appraisal`

-- The five things the first sentence asks of a claimant. Two of them are the outcomes of other provisions:
-- "otherwise complied with subsection (d)" is decided by the rules of dg7-appraisal-procedure.l4 (this module cannot import
-- it, because the procedure rules ask which shares carry appraisal rights, which is decided here), and "consented
-- thereto in writing pursuant to s 228" is a fact about a consent given under s 228 (out of range: section 228, piece dg5).
-- src:1252 | Any stockholder of a corporation of this State who holds shares of stock on the date of the making of a demand pursuant to subsection (d) of this section with respect to such shares, who continuously holds such shares through the effective date of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, who has otherwise complied with subsection (d) of this section and who has neither voted in favor of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance nor consented thereto in writing pursuant to § 228 of this title shall be entitled to an appraisal by the Court of Chancery of the fair value of the stockholder’s shares of stock under the circumstances described in subsections (b) and (c) of this section …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(a) (src:1252)
DECLARE `s 262(a) Claimant` HAS
    `the stock is stock of a corporation formed`                                    IS A `Where an entity is formed`
    `the claimant holds the stock as holder of record`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `held shares of stock on the date of the making of the demand`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `continuously held the shares through the effective date`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `has otherwise complied with subsection (d)`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `voted in favor of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consented to it in writing pursuant to s 228`                                  IS A BOOLEAN

-- Everything in the first sentence except being a holder of record. A beneficial owner who demands under
-- paragraph (d)(3) must "otherwise satisfy the requirements applicable to a stockholder under the first sentence of
-- subsection (a)", so (d)(3) reads this rule, and the stockholder's rule below adds the holder-of-record limb.
-- src:1252 | Any stockholder of a corporation of this State who holds shares of stock on the date of the making of a demand pursuant to subsection (d) of this section with respect to such shares, who continuously holds such shares through the effective date of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, who has otherwise complied with subsection (d) of this section and who has neither voted in favor of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance nor consented thereto in writing pursuant to § 228 of this title shall be entitled to an appraisal by the Court of Chancery of the fair value of the stockholder’s shares of stock under the circumstances described in subsections (b) and (c) of this section …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(a) (src:1252)
GIVEN c IS A `s 262(a) Claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(a) the claimant meets the conditions of the first sentence other than holding of record` c MEANS
        c's `the stock is stock of a corporation formed` EQUALS `this State`
    AND c's `held shares of stock on the date of the making of the demand`
    AND c's `continuously held the shares through the effective date`
    AND c's `has otherwise complied with subsection (d)`
    AND (NOT c's `voted in favor of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance`)
    AND (NOT c's `consented to it in writing pursuant to s 228`)

-- "shall be entitled to an appraisal by the Court of Chancery of the fair value of the stockholder's shares of stock
-- under the circumstances described in subsections (b) and (c) of this section".
-- The circumstances are the outcome of `s 262 appraisal rights are available for the shares` below, taken here as an input
-- so that this rule can be read on its own.
-- src:1252 | shall be entitled to an appraisal by the Court of Chancery of the fair value of the stockholder’s shares of stock under the circumstances described in subsections (b) and (c) of this section …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(a) (src:1252)
GIVEN c IS A `s 262(a) Claimant`
      `the circumstances described in subsections (b) and (c) exist` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(a) the stockholder is entitled to an appraisal of the fair value of the shares` c `the circumstances described in subsections (b) and (c) exist` MEANS
        c's `the claimant holds the stock as holder of record`
    AND `s 262(a) the claimant meets the conditions of the first sentence other than holding of record` c
    AND `the circumstances described in subsections (b) and (c) exist`

§ `s 262(b) For which shares appraisal rights are available`

-- How the transaction was approved decides both the date at which paragraph (b)(1) tests the class or series
-- and which notice paragraph of subsection (d) applies. The five routes are those the text names:
-- a meeting of stockholders (paragraph (d)(1)), and approval pursuant to s 228, s 251(h), s 253 or s 267 (paragraph (d)(2)).
-- src:1254 | at the record date fixed to determine the stockholders entitled to receive notice of the meeting of stockholders, or at the record date fixed to determine the stockholders entitled to consent pursuant to § 228 of this title …
-- src:1265 | If the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance was approved pursuant to § 228, § 251(h), § 253, or § 267 of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(b)(1) (src:1254); § 262(d)(2) (src:1265)
DECLARE `s 262 How the transaction was approved` IS ONE OF
    `approved at a meeting of stockholders`
    `approved by consent of stockholders pursuant to s 228`
    `approved pursuant to s 251(h)`
    `approved pursuant to s 253`
    `approved pursuant to s 267`

-- The date at which paragraph (b)(1) looks at the class or series.
-- src:1254 | at the record date fixed to determine the stockholders entitled to receive notice of the meeting of stockholders, or at the record date fixed to determine the stockholders entitled to consent pursuant to § 228 of this title, to act upon the agreement of merger or consolidation or the resolution providing for the conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance (or, in the case of a merger pursuant to § 251(h) of this title, as of immediately prior to the execution of the agreement of merger …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(b)(1) (src:1254)
DECLARE `s 262(b)(1) The time at which the class or series is tested` IS ONE OF
    `the record date fixed to determine the stockholders entitled to receive notice of the meeting`
    `the record date fixed to determine the stockholders entitled to consent pursuant to s 228`
    `immediately prior to the execution of the agreement of merger under s 251(h)`

-- A merger approved under s 253 or s 267 has neither a meeting nor a consent nor an s 251(h) agreement, so the text
-- names no time for it: NOTHING (not covered). That is harmless: s 253 and s 267 mergers are not in the list of
-- subsection (b) at all, and paragraph (b)(3) governs them.
-- src:1254 | at the record date fixed to determine the stockholders entitled to receive notice of the meeting of stockholders, or at the record date fixed to determine the stockholders entitled to consent pursuant to § 228 of this title, to act upon the agreement of merger or consolidation or the resolution providing for the conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance (or, in the case of a merger pursuant to § 251(h) of this title, as of immediately prior to the execution of the agreement of merger …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(b)(1) (src:1254)
GIVEN a IS A `s 262 How the transaction was approved`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 262(b)(1) The time at which the class or series is tested`
`s 262(b)(1) the time at which the class or series is tested` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `approved at a meeting of stockholders`                     THEN JUST `the record date fixed to determine the stockholders entitled to receive notice of the meeting`
    WHEN `approved by consent of stockholders pursuant to s 228`     THEN JUST `the record date fixed to determine the stockholders entitled to consent pursuant to s 228`
    WHEN `approved pursuant to s 251(h)`                             THEN JUST `immediately prior to the execution of the agreement of merger under s 251(h)`
    WHEN `approved pursuant to s 253`                                THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `approved pursuant to s 267`                                THEN NOTHING

-- Which of the transactions the text lists. The list: s 251 (other than a merger under s 251(g)), s 252, s 254, s 255,
-- s 256, s 257, s 258, s 263, s 264, s 266, s 390. A merger under s 253 or s 267 is not on it (paragraph (b)(3) gives
-- the subsidiary's stockholders appraisal rights in that case only).
-- src:1253 | Appraisal rights shall be available for the shares of any class or series of stock of a constituent, converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation in a merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance to be effected pursuant to § 251 (other than a merger effected pursuant to § 251(g) of this title), § 252, § 254, § 255, § 256, § 257, § 258, § 263, § 264, § 266 or § 390 of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(b) (src:1253)
GIVEN p IS A `dg7 Provision under which a transaction is effected`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(b) the provision is one of those the subsection lists` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `a merger or consolidation under s 251 other than a merger under s 251(g)`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a merger under s 251(g)`                                                   THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a merger or consolidation under s 252`                                     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a merger of a parent corporation and its subsidiary under s 253`           THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a merger or consolidation under s 254`                                     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a merger or consolidation under s 255`                                     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a merger or consolidation under s 256`                                     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a merger or consolidation under s 257`                                     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a merger or consolidation under s 258`                                     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a merger or consolidation under s 263`                                     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a merger or consolidation under s 264`                                     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a conversion under s 266`                                                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a merger of a parent entity and its subsidiary under s 267`                THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a transfer, domestication or continuance under s 390`                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a transaction effected under none of the provisions that s 261 and s 262 name` THEN FALSE

-- The words in brackets after the list: "(other than, in each case and solely with respect to a converted or domesticated
-- corporation, a merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance authorized pursuant to and in
-- accordance with the provisions of s 265 or s 388)". Read as two facts: the shares are those of a converted or
-- domesticated corporation, and the transaction is authorized pursuant to and in accordance with s 265 or s 388.
-- src:1253 | (other than, in each case and solely with respect to a converted or domesticated corporation, a merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance authorized pursuant to and in accordance with the provisions of § 265 or § 388 of this title) …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(b) (src:1253)
GIVEN `the shares are those of a converted or domesticated corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is authorized pursuant to and in accordance with the provisions of s 265 or s 388` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(b) the transaction is excepted as one under s 265 or s 388 of a converted or domesticated corporation` `the shares are those of a converted or domesticated corporation` `the transaction is authorized pursuant to and in accordance with the provisions of s 265 or s 388` MEANS
        `the shares are those of a converted or domesticated corporation`
    AND `the transaction is authorized pursuant to and in accordance with the provisions of s 265 or s 388`

-- Paragraph (b)(1), first proviso: "no appraisal rights ... shall be available for the shares of any class or series of stock,
-- which stock, or depository receipts in respect thereof, at the record date ... were either: (i) listed on a national
-- securities exchange or (ii) held of record by more than 2,000 holders". "More than 2,000" is exclusive: 2,000 holders
-- is not enough, 2,001 is.
-- src:1254 | (1) Provided, however, that no appraisal rights under this section shall be available for the shares of any class or series of stock, which stock, or depository receipts in respect thereof, at the record date fixed to determine the stockholders entitled to receive notice of the meeting of stockholders, or at the record date fixed to determine the stockholders entitled to consent pursuant to § 228 of this title, to act upon the agreement of merger or consolidation or the resolution providing for the conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance (or, in the case of a merger pursuant to § 251(h) of this title, as of immediately prior to the execution of the agreement of merger), were either: (i) listed on a national securities exchange or (ii) held of record by more than 2,000 holders …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(b)(1) (src:1254)
GIVEN `the stock or the depository receipts in respect of it were listed on a national securities exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of holders of record of the stock or the depository receipts` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(b)(1) the class or series was listed or held of record by more than 2,000 holders` `the stock or the depository receipts in respect of it were listed on a national securities exchange` `the number of holders of record of the stock or the depository receipts` MEANS
        `the stock or the depository receipts in respect of it were listed on a national securities exchange`
    OR `the number of holders of record of the stock or the depository receipts` GREATER THAN 2000

-- Paragraph (b)(1), second proviso: "no appraisal rights shall be available for any shares of stock of the constituent
-- corporation surviving a merger if the merger did not require for its approval the vote of the stockholders of the
-- surviving corporation as provided in s 251(f)" (out of range: section 251(f), piece dg6).
-- src:1254 | and further provided that no appraisal rights shall be available for any shares of stock of the constituent corporation surviving a merger if the merger did not require for its approval the vote of the stockholders of the surviving corporation as provided in § 251(f) of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(b)(1) (src:1254)
GIVEN `the shares are those of the constituent corporation surviving the merger` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the merger did not require for its approval the vote of the stockholders of the surviving corporation as provided in s 251(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(b)(1) the shares are those of a surviving corporation whose stockholders did not vote under s 251(f)` `the shares are those of the constituent corporation surviving the merger` `the merger did not require for its approval the vote of the stockholders of the surviving corporation as provided in s 251(f)` MEANS
        `the shares are those of the constituent corporation surviving the merger`
    AND `the merger did not require for its approval the vote of the stockholders of the surviving corporation as provided in s 251(f)`

-- Paragraph (b)(2). Subparagraphs a. to d. say what the holders may be required to accept without having appraisal
-- rights restored; anything else restores them "notwithstanding paragraph (b)(1)".
-- src:1255 | (2) Notwithstanding paragraph (b)(1) of this section, appraisal rights under this section shall be available for the shares of any class or series of stock of a constituent, converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation if the holders thereof are required by the terms of an agreement of merger or consolidation, or by the terms of a resolution providing for conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, pursuant to § 251, § 252, § 254, § 255, § 256, § 257, § 258, § 263, § 264, § 266 or § 390 of this title to accept for such stock anything except:
