    `the parent owns all of the stock of the subsidiary Delaware corporation immediately prior to the merger` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Subsection (b) as a whole. The structure of the text is: the list (with the bracketed exception); then (b)(1) takes
-- away appraisal rights from a listed or widely held class or series, and from the shares of a surviving corporation
-- whose stockholders did not vote; then (b)(2), "notwithstanding paragraph (b)(1)", restores them if the holders must
-- accept anything but a. to d.; and (b)(3) adds the subsidiary of a s 253 or s 267 merger.
-- FORK F-b1: (b)(2) says "notwithstanding paragraph (b)(1)", the whole paragraph, so it is read as overriding BOTH
-- provisos of (b)(1). (The second proviso then never bites in practice: a surviving corporation's stockholders keep
-- identical shares, so (b)(2) is not triggered for them.)
-- src:1253 | Appraisal rights shall be available for the shares of any class or series of stock of a constituent, converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation in a merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance to be effected pursuant to § 251 (other than a merger effected pursuant to § 251(g) of this title), § 252, § 254, § 255, § 256, § 257, § 258, § 263, § 264, § 266 or § 390 of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(b) (src:1253)
GIVEN t IS A `s 262(b) Class or series in a transaction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(b) appraisal rights are available for the class or series` t MEANS
        (       `the transaction is on the list and is not excepted`
          AND (   NOT `paragraph (b)(1) takes appraisal rights away`
               OR `paragraph (b)(2) restores appraisal rights`))
    OR `paragraph (b)(3) gives appraisal rights to the subsidiary`
    WHERE
        `the transaction is on the list and is not excepted` MEANS
                `s 262(b) the provision is one of those the subsection lists` (t's `the provision under which the transaction is effected`)
            AND (NOT `s 262(b) the transaction is excepted as one under s 265 or s 388 of a converted or domesticated corporation` (t's `the shares are those of a converted or domesticated corporation`) (t's `the transaction is authorized pursuant to and in accordance with the provisions of s 265 or s 388`))
        `paragraph (b)(1) takes appraisal rights away` MEANS
                `s 262(b)(1) the class or series was listed or held of record by more than 2,000 holders` (t's `the stock or the depository receipts in respect of it were listed on a national securities exchange`) (t's `the number of holders of record of the stock or the depository receipts`)
             OR `s 262(b)(1) the shares are those of a surviving corporation whose stockholders did not vote under s 251(f)` (t's `the shares are those of the constituent corporation surviving the merger`) (t's `the merger did not require for its approval the vote of the stockholders of the surviving corporation as provided in s 251(f)`)
        `paragraph (b)(2) restores appraisal rights` MEANS
            `s 262(b)(2) the holders are required to accept something other than what a. to d. describe` (t's `what the holders are required to accept`)
        `paragraph (b)(3) gives appraisal rights to the subsidiary` MEANS
            `s 262(b)(3) appraisal rights are available for the shares of the subsidiary Delaware corporation` (t's `the provision under which the transaction is effected`) (t's `the parent owns all of the stock of the subsidiary Delaware corporation immediately prior to the merger`)

§ `s 262(c) Appraisal rights a certificate of incorporation provides`

-- "Any corporation may provide in its certificate of incorporation that appraisal rights under this section shall be
-- available for the shares of any class or series of its stock as a result of" one of five events.
-- src:1262 | (c) Any corporation may provide in its certificate of incorporation that appraisal rights under this section shall be available for the shares of any class or series of its stock as a result of an amendment to its certificate of incorporation, any merger or consolidation in which the corporation is a constituent corporation, the sale of all or substantially all of the assets of the corporation or a conversion effected pursuant to § 266 of this title or a transfer, domestication or continuance effected pursuant to § 390 of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(c) (src:1262)
DECLARE `s 262(c) Event for which the certificate may provide appraisal rights` IS ONE OF
    `an amendment to its certificate of incorporation`
    `any merger or consolidation in which the corporation is a constituent corporation`
    `the sale of all or substantially all of the assets of the corporation`
    `a conversion effected pursuant to s 266`
    `a transfer, domestication or continuance effected pursuant to s 390`

-- The certificate provides appraisal rights for the event the class or series now faces.
-- src:1262 | (c) Any corporation may provide in its certificate of incorporation that appraisal rights under this section shall be available for the shares of any class or series of its stock as a result of an amendment to its certificate of incorporation, any merger or consolidation in which the corporation is a constituent corporation, the sale of all or substantially all of the assets of the corporation or a conversion effected pursuant to § 266 of this title or a transfer, domestication or continuance effected pursuant to § 390 of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(c) (src:1262)
GIVEN `the events for which the certificate of incorporation provides appraisal rights` IS A LIST OF `s 262(c) Event for which the certificate may provide appraisal rights`
      `the event the class or series faces` IS A `s 262(c) Event for which the certificate may provide appraisal rights`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(c) appraisal rights are available because the certificate of incorporation so provides` `the events for which the certificate of incorporation provides appraisal rights` `the event the class or series faces` MEANS
    elem `the event the class or series faces` `the events for which the certificate of incorporation provides appraisal rights`

-- "If the certificate of incorporation contains such a provision, the provisions of this section, including those set forth
-- in subsections (d), (e), and (g) of this section, shall apply as nearly as is practicable." What is practicable is not a
-- matter this encoding can decide, so the rule records only that the provision brings the section in: the rules of
-- dg7-appraisal-procedure.l4 and dg7-appraisal-proceeding.l4 are then read for the shares, and where one cannot be read
-- literally (for example the references to a merger agreement in a sale of assets) the reader decides what is practicable.
